  "concrete_finding": {
    "status": "Corrected in selected v2; predecessor and finding retained unchanged.",
    "counterexample": [
      "verification/Foo/a.raw",
      "verification/foo/b.raw"
    ],
    "old_behavior": "When their shared parent was absent from the committed tree, the predecessor compared each prefix only with existing_spelling and did not remember newly planned prefixes. Whole target uniqueness and file/ancestor checks did not reject the conflicting new parent spellings before copying.",
    "selected_correction": "A separate planned_spelling copy admits and records each existing/planned parent and full target prefix before any source/index write. existing_spelling is unchanged and remains the authority for new-target absence checks.",
    "actual_copy_plan": "The immutable E2B plan has no conflicting prefix spellings among its 244 core targets including the manifest; this source defect concerns the generic future-manifest gate.",
    "verification": "The exact one-hunk forward/full inverse and all other bytes are verified. Independent prefix comparisons use inert path data only; the adapter was not evaluated."
  },
  "semantic_findings": [
    {
      "area": "Future release and schema",
      "assessment": "The four unresolved bindings are still the released head, final manifest path, raw manifest SHA-256 and positive complete path count. Disabled assertions and unresolved bindings are rejected before CLI/repository admission. A later Root release must pin the actual bound adapter and manifest, branch/head, required current acceptance pins and exact object format; source review is not that release."
    },
    {
      "area": "Canonical targets and ownership of bytes",
      "assessment": "Every physical row including the synthetic manifest passes canonical Windows path, prefix spelling, file/directory collision, reparse, mode, containment, donor and preimage/absence gates. Existing modes are preserved; additions require 100644. Both BASIS and current-head raw blobs must equal the actual replacement preimage."
    },
    {
      "area": "All donor aliases",
      "assessment": "Every explicit alias is pinned and compared byte-for-byte with its physical row. Primary membership and duplicate target/canonical-donor/size/hash identities are enforced; the synthetic manifest gets its own alias record and participates in the complete byte contract. The semantic completeness of the later final manifest and its historical reference records remains a separate manifest-peer/Root responsibility."
    },
    {
      "area": "Attributes and conversion provenance",
      "assessment": "The full target list receives text, eol, filter, working-tree-encoding and ident checks. Disallowed filter/encoding/ident values are rejected before the first path-aware hash. Relevant Git configuration is captured with includes, origin and scope; system/global/info/root/target-ancestor attribute files retain exact bytes or absence and path identities. No donor normalization or attribute editing is performed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Both Git object IDs",
      "assessment": "The repository object format selects the independent raw blob header/content digest. Each exact binary donor must match both Git --no-filters and Git --path identities, without -w. This applies to source, archive, extra final rows and the manifest. SHA-1/SHA-256 raw helper support does not widen the project's exact forty-hex BASIS contract."
    },
    {
      "area": "Ordering before Main/index writes",
      "assessment": "All donor/preimage/alias/path/attribute/object checks complete for the whole manifest before copying. Repository/provenance/head/clean/no-hook checks are repeated and immutable preflight is saved first. No helper invocation from the candidate was used to infer this ordering."
    },
    {
      "area": "Copy, stage and commit",
      "assessment": "Copied bytes are reread and conversion provenance revalidated before literal NUL-list staging. Complete staged names, stage zero, modes, expected object IDs and raw blobs must match. Before commit the same provenance/head/no-hook gates remain. The committed complete parent list must equal exactly [prior_head], with exact changed paths, modes, raw IDs/blobs and checkout bytes, followed by final provenance and clean-worktree checks."
    },
    {
      "area": "Failure record",
      "assessment": "After release and receipt-namespace admission, the failure hook preserves a unique immutable negative containing stage, error/traceback and write-start state; no rollback or cleanup occurs. Earlier unresolved/release/namespace failures precede the hook and require Root preservation of the original tool/job result, as stated in the contract."
    }
  ],
